Overlay patch 0025: thread-safe CVar map (reference 0030 = SYNC WAVE 2
item 1, CRITICAL — latent crash every port ships). SpaghettiKart has the
exact architecture that SEGV'd the Ship of Harkinian port: GameEngine::HandleAudioThread
reads CVarGetFloat("gGameMasterVolume") EVERY audio frame (Engine.cpp:504)
while the main thread writes CVars (menu interaction, race transitions) —
ConsoleVariable::mVariables is a bare unordered_map, and a concurrent
insert can rehash while the audio thread is inside find() → freed-bucket
deref → SEGV. Fix: recursive_mutex over every mVariables access (reads
funnel through Get(); writes are the five Set*, ClearVariable,
CopyVariable, Save, Load). Recursive because Register*/ClearVariable/Load
re-enter via Get()/Set*(). Uncontended cost is tens of ns — noise.
Sole pin delta vs the Ship of Harkinian port patch: Context::GetInstance (pre-rename)
in ClearVariable/Save/Load context lines. Residual (reference-documented):
GetString's char* after a concurrent SetString — no audio-thread string
reads exist in this port either (master volume is a float).

